    {
      "section": "content.media-split",
      "variant": "text-left",
      "content": {
        "eyebrow": "One engine, everywhere",
        "title": "The engine that powers it all",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The open engine inside Lattice reads your project, works out the dependency graph and compiles every model into SQL your warehouse understands. It runs the same way on a laptop, in a scheduled job or inside an agent workflow, so what you preview while building matches exactly what runs in production.",
          "Most teams start on **the open-source engine** and add the hosted platform as they grow."
        ],
        "primary": {
          "label": "Install the engine",
          "href": "/learn"
        },
        "tertiary": {
          "label": "Read docs",
          "href": "/learn"
        },
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
          "alt": "Metric card with a trend line and its YAML definition",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/hero/semantic-layer.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "columns": "6/6",
        "topPadding": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "content.media-split",
      "variant": "text-left",
      "content": {
        "eyebrow": "Hosted platform",
        "title": "Run the engine with a full team around it",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The hosted platform adds what a growing team needs around the engine: a browser editor and visual canvas, scheduled jobs, alerts, a searchable catalog, governed metrics and an assistant that knows your project. Administrators get single sign-on, permissions and audit logs too."
        ],
        "primary": {
          "label": "Try it free",
          "href": "/signup"
        },
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
          "alt": "Five team projects connected around a shared finance project",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/hero/mesh.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "columns": "6/6",
        "topPadding": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "social-proof.customer-tabs",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "title": "Proof from real teams",
        "stories": [
          {
            "name": "Kestrel",
            "logo": {
              "assetRole": "customer.logo",
              "alt": "Kestrel",
              "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-1.svg"
            },
            "headline": "Kestrel halves nightly build time with Lattice",
            "summary": "Kestrel moved four hundred production models onto state-aware builds and rebuilt its review process around small pull requests, cutting run times and catching issues sooner.",
            "quote": "We used to watch the nightly load creep past breakfast while everyone argued about which dashboard to believe. Moving the project onto Lattice changed both of those problems at once. Only the models that actually changed are rebuilt, every number arrives before the first meeting, and when something looks wrong we can trace it to a specific commit in minutes.",
            "person": "Priya Raman",
            "role": "Head of Analytics Engineering",
            "stats": [
              {
                "number": "52%",
                "label": "shorter nightly runs after the move to state-aware builds"
              },
              {
                "number": "2.5x",
                "label": "more models shipped each sprint with tests and docs"
              }
            ],
            "action": {
              "label": "Read customer story",
              "href": "/case-studies/kestrel"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Meridian Partners",
            "logo": {
              "assetRole": "customer.logo",
              "alt": "Meridian Partners",
              "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-2.svg"
            },
            "headline": "One set of figures for eleven regional desks",
            "summary": "Meridian Partners replaced eleven separate spreadsheets of portfolio logic with one governed project, so every desk reports the same assets under management on the same day.",
            "quote": "Closing each quarter once meant a week spent matching up eleven competing copies of one number. Today there is one tested definition that every desk reads from, and the conversation at the end of the quarter is about what the numbers mean rather than which spreadsheet is right. The audit team noticed the difference before we had even announced it.",
            "person": "Tomas Ekberg",
            "role": "Director of Data Platforms",
            "stats": [
              {
                "number": "11",
                "label": "regional desks reporting from one governed project"
              },
              {
                "number": "4d",
                "label": "saved on every quarterly close with no manual reconciling"
              }
            ],
            "action": {
              "label": "Read customer story",
              "href": "/case-studies/meridian-partners"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Tidepool",
            "logo": {
              "assetRole": "customer.logo",
              "alt": "Tidepool",
              "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-3.svg"
            },
            "headline": "Self-serve answers for every product squad",
            "summary": "Tidepool gave product managers documented, tested models to build on, which cut the queue of ad hoc requests and freed a small data team to work on new questions.",
            "quote": "Product managers wanted answers in hours, and our tiny data team was drowning in tickets. Once the core models were documented and tested in Lattice, people could find what they needed and trust it without asking us first. We still get questions, but they are better questions, and we finally have time to work on the ideas that move the business forward.",
            "person": "Ana Kowalski",
            "role": "Staff Data Engineer",
            "stats": [
              {
                "number": "70%",
                "label": "fewer ad hoc requests reaching the central data team"
              },
              {
                "number": "140",
                "label": "dashboards rebuilt on certified, documented models"
              }
            ],
            "action": {
              "label": "Read customer story",
              "href": "/case-studies"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Orbitly",
            "logo": {
              "assetRole": "customer.logo",
              "alt": "Orbitly",
              "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-5.svg"
            },
            "headline": "Lower warehouse spend while shipping more models",
            "summary": "Orbitly reused results for unchanged models and moved heavy transformations to incremental builds, bringing compute spend down in the first month after migrating.",
            "quote": "Our compute bill was growing faster than the team, and nobody could say which models were responsible. Lattice showed us exactly what ran, how long it took and what it cost, and state-aware builds stopped us paying to rebuild tables that had not changed. The same project now serves twice as many teams, and finance stopped sending us worried messages.",
            "person": "Jonah Reyes",
            "role": "VP, Data and Insights",
            "stats": [
              {
                "number": "62%",
                "label": "lower warehouse spend after moving to state-aware builds"
              },
              {
                "number": "2x",
                "label": "as many teams served from one project with no new hires"
              }
            ],
            "action": {
              "label": "Read customer story",
              "href": "/case-studies"
            }
          }
        ]
